[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have this theorem somewhere?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Monoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toMonoidHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 597312274,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1779545940
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulEquiv.coe_toMonoidHom#doc\">docs#MulEquiv.coe_toMonoidHom</a> help?</p>",
        "id": 597312447,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1779546078
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah that one is close but it doesn't close this goal</p>",
        "id": 597312473,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1779546101
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we not have this for all <code>EquivLike</code> stuffs? (but even we do I think it's still somewhat helpful to have it in each <code>XEquiv</code> namespace)</p>",
        "id": 597312500,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1779546124
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think we usually only add the <code>⇑FooHom.toBarHom f = ⇑f</code> lemma, which is typically the more useful one.</p>",
        "id": 597312634,
        "sender_full_name": "Christian Merten",
        "timestamp": 1779546252
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>by simp</code> solves this, by <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulEquiv.toMonoidHom_eq_coe#doc\">docs#MulEquiv.toMonoidHom_eq_coe</a> + <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MonoidHom.coe_coe#doc\">docs#MonoidHom.coe_coe</a></p>",
        "id": 597312709,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779546341
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We can't have every <code>rfl</code> theorem, there are just too many possibilities. But we should add everything we need for <code>simp</code> to solve them, which is still a lot but not a lot a lot.</p>",
        "id": 597312937,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779546521
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"648495\">Christian Merten</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/MulEquiv.2EtoMonoidHom_apply/near/597312634\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think we usually only add the <code>⇑FooHom.toBarHom f = ⇑f</code> lemma, which is typically the more useful one.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I agree that it's useful but I would say the lemma I wrote is useful in goals like <code>e (e.symm.toXHom x) = x</code>.</p>",
        "id": 597312938,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1779546522
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does <code>simp</code> not solve such a goal?</p>",
        "id": 597312949,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779546539
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/MulEquiv.2EtoMonoidHom_apply/near/597312949\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Does <code>simp</code> not solve such a goal?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>not if you do <code>let f : X →* Y := e.symm.toXHom</code></p>",
        "id": 597313072,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1779546606
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>simp +zetaDelta</code> would though</p>",
        "id": 597313097,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1779546629
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And <code>simp [f]</code>?</p>",
